# Theme Customization Guidelines

## SCSS Structure
The theme uses SCSS for styling with the following structure:
- `_sass/_base.scss` - Base styles and typography
- `_sass/_cv.scss` - CV/resume specific styles
- `_sass/_distill.scss` - Distill post styles
- `_sass/font-awesome/` - Font Awesome icon styles
- `_sass/tabler-icons/` - Tabler icon styles

## Customization Points

### Colors and Typography
Modify `_sass/_base.scss` for:
- Primary and secondary colors
- Font families and sizes
- Link colors and hover states
- Background colors

### Layout Modifications
- **Header**: Edit `_includes/header.liquid`
- **Footer**: Edit `_includes/footer.liquid`
- **Navigation**: Modify navigation structure in header
- **Sidebar**: Customize sidebar components

### Component Styling
- **Posts**: Customize `_layouts/post.liquid`
- **Pages**: Modify `_layouts/page.liquid`
- **Projects**: Edit `_layouts/profiles.liquid`
- **CV**: Update `_layouts/cv.liquid`

## Asset Management
- **Images**: Store in `assets/img/`
- **CSS**: Custom styles in `assets/css/`
- **JavaScript**: Custom scripts in `assets/js/`
- **Fonts**: Web fonts in `assets/fonts/`

## Icon Usage
- **Font Awesome**: Use Font Awesome icons for general UI
- **Tabler Icons**: Use Tabler icons for modern interface elements
- **Academic Icons**: Use academicons for academic-specific icons

## Responsive Design
- Follow mobile-first approach
- Test on various screen sizes
- Use Bootstrap grid system
- Ensure accessibility compliance

## Custom Components
Create reusable components in `_includes/`:
- Custom figure layouts
- Specialized content blocks
- Interactive elements
- Social media integrations

## Performance Optimization
- Minimize CSS and JavaScript
- Optimize images and assets
- Use CDN for external resources
- Implement lazy loading where appropriate

## Key Style Files
- [base.scss](mdc:_sass/_base.scss) - Main styling foundation
- [cv.scss](mdc:_sass/_cv.scss) - CV page styles
- [distill.scss](mdc:_sass/_distill.scss) - Distill post styles
